#: ../../../gpu-programming/virtual-memory-and-peer-access.md:500
msgid "Do not wrap VMM pointers in an owning buffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/virtual-memory-and-peer-access.md:502
msgid ""
"A VMM virtual address is owned by its `Mapping`, `VirtualReservation`, and "
"`PhysicalAllocation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/virtual-memory-and-peer-access.md:505
msgid ""
"Do not construct an owning `DeviceBuffer` from that pointer unless the API "
"explicitly defines a non-owning conversion. An owning buffer could attempt "
"to release the pointer using `cuMemFree`, while the VMM resources expect "
"`cuMemUnmap`, `cuMemAddressFree`, and `cuMemRelease`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/virtual-memory-and-peer-access.md:510
msgid ""
"Pass the raw `CUdeviceptr` only to APIs that accept non-owning device "
"addresses."
